IMPORT prelude

-- Military Manoeuvres Act 1905 (Singapore) -- notice of manoeuvres (s 2), what troops may and may not enter or take (s 3),
-- compensation for damage and its time limit (ss 4, 5), offences during manoeuvres (s 6), waterworks catchments (s 7), the
-- powers on a declared manoeuvring or firing ground (ss 9, 10), rules for firing grounds and Parliament's approval of rules
-- affecting public rights (s 11), and firing-ground compensation, its form and its time limit (ss 12 to 14).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 28/10/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MMA1905.txt. The cover says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 24 of 2022 wef 28/10/2022 (s 7, the Public Utilities
-- Board's approval). The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is one line out of step with the body; the body's
-- numbering is followed.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0136 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (14 sections), so nearly all of it is encoded. Not encoded: the Minister's power to proclaim
-- grounds (s 8) beyond taking "declared" as a given fact; the content of any rules actually made under s 11 (none was retrieved);
-- the arbitration procedure under the Arbitration Act beyond the reference to 2 arbitrators; the size of any compensation.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Military Manoeuvres Act 1905 -- manoeuvres, firing grounds and compensation`

§§ `2 -- notice of manoeuvres`

-- s 2(1): "Whenever the number of troops to be engaged in military manoeuvres exceeds 500, notice in writing shall be given to the
-- secretary to the Armed Forces Council at least one month before" the manoeuvres, specifying (a) the commencement date, "the
-- period not exceeding 3 months" and approximately the limits; and (b) "a date not earlier than one month from the conclusion of
-- the manoeuvres" by which compensation claims are to be sent.
-- s 2(2): copies posted "in every village and at other convenient places within the limits ... at least 14 days before" the start.
-- s 2(3): where the troops do "not exceed 500 no such notice ... shall be necessary; and if no such notice is given, the
-- manoeuvres shall not extend beyond a period of 48 hours".
-- s 9(1)(a): on a declared manoeuvring ground the Armed Forces Council may direct manoeuvres "without giving the notice required
-- by section 2".
GIVEN `troops engaged` IS A NUMBER, `on a declared manoeuvring ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice to the Armed Forces Council is required` IF
    `troops engaged` GREATER THAN 500 AND (NOT `on a declared manoeuvring ground`)

GIVEN `months of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice was given early enough` IF `months of notice` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `notified period in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notified period is within the limit` IF `notified period in months` AT MOST 3

GIVEN `days posted before commencement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice was posted in time` IF `days posted before commencement` AT LEAST 14

GIVEN `claims date in months after conclusion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claims date in the notice is lawful` IF `claims date in months after conclusion` AT LEAST 1

-- INFERENCE: the 48-hour cap in s 2(3) is attached to manoeuvres of 500 or fewer troops held without notice. Manoeuvres
-- directed on a declared manoeuvring ground under s 9(1)(a) are freed from the notice, and the text does not apply the 48-hour
-- cap to them; this encoding treats them as uncapped.
GIVEN `troops engaged` IS A NUMBER, `hours of manoeuvres` IS A NUMBER, `on a declared manoeuvring ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `manoeuvres without notice stay within the Act` IF
        `on a declared manoeuvring ground`
    OR  (`troops engaged` AT MOST 500 AND `hours of manoeuvres` AT MOST 48)

§§ `3 -- what the troops may do`

-- s 3(1): within the notified limits "and during the specified period", the troops may (a) "pass over and encamp, construct
-- military works not of a permanent character and execute military manoeuvres on any land"; and (b) take water "from any
-- sources of water, public or private, and for that purpose dam up any running water", "provided that such damming ... does not
-- interfere with any trade or industry" and that nothing authorises taking water from a private owner's or public authority's
-- supply "except subject to the supply shown to be required by those entitled to use the water supply".
-- s 3(2): "Nothing in this Act shall authorise entry on or interference with any dwelling house, place of worship, school,
-- factory, store or premises used for the carrying on of any business or manufacture or any ground attached to any place of
-- worship or school or any premises enclosed within the curtilage of or attached to any dwelling house."
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `an open field`
    `vacant land`
    `a dwelling house`
    `a garden within the curtilage of a dwelling house`
    `a place of worship`
    `ground attached to a place of worship`
    `a school`
    `ground attached to a school`
    `a factory`
    `a shop`

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is protected` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `an open field` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `vacant land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `within the notified limits and period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the troops may enter` IF
    `within the notified limits and period` AND (NOT `the place is protected` `the place`)

GIVEN `the work is permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the troops may construct the work` IF NOT `the work is permanent`

GIVEN `the damming interferes with a trade or industry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the troops may dam the running water` IF NOT `the damming interferes with a trade or industry`

GIVEN `the supply belongs to a private owner or public authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the needs shown by those entitled are still met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the troops may take water from the source` IF
        (NOT `the supply belongs to a private owner or public authority`)
    OR  `the needs shown by those entitled are still met`

§§ `4, 5, 11(3), 12 -- which compensation applies`

-- s 4(1): "Full compensation shall be paid for any injury or damage to persons or property or interference with rights or
-- privileges arising from putting in force any of the provisions of this Act, whether or not occasioned by the acts or defaults
-- of the forces", including "all expenses reasonably incurred in the protection of persons, property, rights and privileges, and
-- any damage by reason of excessive weight or extraordinary traffic caused to any highway".
-- s 11(3): rules that "injuriously affect or obstruct the exercise of any private right of any person in or over any sea, tidal
-- water or shore" carry compensation.
-- s 12: owners or occupiers of land in a firing ground are compensated "for any loss or damage arising from the land ... being
-- proclaimed a firing ground", "independent of and in addition to" s 4 compensation.
DECLARE Loss IS ONE OF
    `personal injury during manoeuvres`
    `crops trampled during manoeuvres`
    `a blocked right of way during manoeuvres`
    `the cost of fencing livestock away from the manoeuvres`
    `a road damaged by heavy military traffic`
    `land losing value by being proclaimed a firing ground`
    `a private fishing right obstructed by firing-ground rules`

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `s 4 full compensation`
    `s 11(3) compensation`
    `s 12 compensation`

GIVEN `the loss` IS A Loss
GIVETH A Route
`the compensation route` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the loss`
    WHEN `land losing value by being proclaimed a firing ground` THEN `s 12 compensation`
    WHEN `a private fishing right obstructed by firing-ground rules` THEN `s 11(3) compensation`
    OTHERWISE `s 4 full compensation`

-- s 4(2): compensation is paid to all who send claims to the secretary "within the period named in the notice or, if there is no
-- such notice, ... within one month from the conclusion of the manoeuvres". Fault is irrelevant (s 4(1), above): the forces'
-- fault is not an input.
GIVEN `a notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `sent by the date named in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sent within one month of the conclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 4 claim is in time` IF
    IF `a notice was given` THEN `sent by the date named in the notice` ELSE `sent within one month of the conclusion`

-- s 5(1), s 13(2): if not "settled by agreement", the difference "shall be referred to arbitration, and the sending in of a claim
-- for compensation shall be treated as a submission to arbitration under the Arbitration Act"; (2), 13(3): "2 arbitrators having
-- power to appoint an umpire".
GIVEN `the amount is agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim goes to arbitration` IF NOT `the amount is agreed`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of arbitrators` MEANS 2

GIVEN `s 4 award` IS A NUMBER, `s 12 award` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total compensation for a firing-ground owner` MEANS `s 4 award` PLUS `s 12 award`

§§ `6 -- offences during manoeuvres`

-- s 6(1): "If within a manoeuvring ground and during the continuance of any military manoeuvres under this Act, any person -- (a)
-- wilfully and unlawfully interferes with the execution of the manoeuvres; (b) without due authority enters or remains in any
-- camp; (c) without due authority moves any flag or other mark ...; or (d) maliciously cuts or damages any telegraph or telephone
-- wire laid down by or for the use of the forces", "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6
-- months or to both". (2): "Such person may be arrested without a warrant" and any animal or vehicle in his charge removed.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `wilfully and unlawfully interfering with the manoeuvres`
    `entering a camp without authority`
    `remaining in a camp without authority`
    `entering a camp with authority`
    `moving a manoeuvre flag without authority`
    `maliciously cutting a field telephone wire`
    `accidentally damaging a field telephone wire`
    `watching the manoeuvres`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is listed in s 6` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `entering a camp with authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `accidentally damaging a field telephone wire` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `watching the manoeuvres` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The offence is confined to conduct "within a manoeuvring ground". INFERENCE: the text does not say whether land within the
-- limits of a s 2 notice that has not been proclaimed under s 8 is a "manoeuvring ground"; this encoding takes the words as they
-- stand and asks whether the place is a manoeuvring ground.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `within a manoeuvring ground` IS A BOOLEAN, `during the manoeuvres` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under s 6` IF
    `within a manoeuvring ground` AND `during the manoeuvres` AND `the conduct is listed in s 6` `the conduct`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS 2000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 6

§§ `7 -- waterworks catchment areas`

-- s 7: "Except with the Public Utilities Board's approval, no military manoeuvres shall be executed and no military encampment made
-- on any land forming part of the catchment area in connection with the impounding reservoir of any public waterworks or on any
-- land set apart for the collection of water for the supply of any public waterworks." [Act 24 of 2022 wef 28/10/2022]
GIVEN `the land is in a waterworks catchment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Public Utilities Board approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `manoeuvres may be held on the land` IF
    (NOT `the land is in a waterworks catchment`) OR `the Public Utilities Board approved`

§§ `10 -- firing exercises`

-- s 10(1)(a): the Armed Forces Council may cause firing exercises on a firing ground "giving not less than 24 hours' notice thereof
-- to the occupiers of land ... by the hoisting of a red flag in a conspicuous position within the firing area"; (b) it may remove
-- buildings, trees or other things that hinder, "and may prohibit the erection of any new building within the firing ground".
GIVEN `hours of notice` IS A NUMBER, `a red flag was hoisted conspicuously` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupiers were given the notice the Act requires` IF
    `hours of notice` AT LEAST 24 AND `a red flag was hoisted conspicuously`

§§ `11 -- rules for firing grounds`

-- s 11(1)(c): the rules may "prescribe a penalty not exceeding $2,000 or 6 months' imprisonment or both".
-- (2): rules published in the Gazette, and copies "in Malay, Chinese, Tamil and English shall be posted in at least 3 conspicuous
-- places within or near the firing ground".
-- (4): rules "which affect any public right shall be presented to Parliament and shall not come into force until approved ... by a
-- resolution of Parliament. ... 'public right' means any right of navigation, anchoring or fishing."
GIVEN `rule fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER, `rule imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule's penalty is within the Act` IF
    `rule fine in dollars` AT MOST 2000 AND `rule imprisonment in months` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `places posted` IS A NUMBER, `posted in all four languages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rules were posted as the Act requires` IF
    `places posted` AT LEAST 3 AND `posted in all four languages`

DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `navigation`
    `anchoring`
    `fishing`
    `swimming`
    `beach walking`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is a public right` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `navigation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anchoring` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `fishing` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the activity restricted` IS AN Activity, `approved by resolution of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule can come into force` IF
    (NOT `the activity is a public right` `the activity restricted`) OR `approved by resolution of Parliament`

§§ `12 to 14 -- firing-ground compensation`

-- s 13(1): "unless otherwise agreed", compensation is "an annual rent payable ... so long as the land ... continues to be a firing
-- ground".
-- s 14(1): claims under s 11(3) or 12 "shall be made in writing to the secretary to the Armed Forces Council, within 2 months after"
-- the land, sea, tidal water or shore "has been used as a firing ground". (2): "No compensation shall be granted for any building
-- erected or commenced after the posting of the rules as provided in section 11(2)."
GIVEN `otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN, `still a firing ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an annual rent is payable` IF (NOT `otherwise agreed`) AND `still a firing ground`

GIVEN `months after use as a firing ground` IS A NUMBER, `made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the firing-ground claim is in time` IF
    `months after use as a firing ground` AT MOST 2 AND `made in writing`

GIVEN `building begun after the rules were posted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation can be granted for the building` IF NOT `building begun after the rules were posted`
